---
description: Go backend conventions for mcpDeck
globs: ["**/*.go", "internal/store/**/*.sql"]
alwaysApply: false
---

Follow AGENTS.md. For Go specifically:

- Test first: failing test tagged `// REQ: <ID>` from docs/requirements.md, then code.
- All outbound HTTP goes through `internal/proxy`. Never create an `http.Client` elsewhere.
- Secrets are injected only in the proxy and must never appear in responses, logs, recordings or errors.
- Stdlib first; explicit constructors; no package-level state; inject clock and ID generator.
- Table-driven tests, `go-cmp`, `t.TempDir()` for SQLite, no `time.Sleep`.
- SQL in `internal/store/queries/*.sql`; regenerate with `make sqlc`.
- Run `make test-go && make lint` before finishing.
